        rules: {
          objective: "Score 250 points through tricks and 'Mariaccio' declarations.",
          gameplay: 'Standard Briscola rules: No obligation to follow suit or trump. High card wins. Winner draws first, then loser, until deck is empty.',
          keyRules: [
            'No obligation to follow suit or trump. High card of led suit wins, or highest trump if any. Winner of trick draws first from stock, then loser. Declare Mariaccio (King and Knight of same suit) when playing one of them for bonus points (40 trump, 20 non-trump). First to 250 points wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize the marriage. A single Trump Marriage (40 pts) is worth more than a natural Ace and 3 combined (21 pts). If you have a King and Knight, save them until you need to snatch the lead.',
          intermediate: "The Lead Management: Don't lead your high point cards (Aces/3s) unless you are sure they won't be trumped. Use small cards (2s/4s) to 'bait' out your opponent's high cards before playing your Mariaccio.",
          advanced: 'Defensive Holding: If your opponent has a high score and is close to 250, try to empty their trump reserves early. Without trumps, their marriages in other suits can still be trumped by you, nullifying their bonus point potential.',
          tips: [
            "Memory: You MUST track the remaining points in the deck as you approach 250. If there are no Aces/3s left, it's very hard to catch up without a marriage.",
            'Call Out: Be bold with the 250-point call. If you are at 240 and you take a King (4 pts) of trumps, you are at 244 plus potentially secret marriages.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
